			  Welcome to The Realm of			        The WizardCommand Line Options:	% castle -h        <* Print this help sheet *>	% castle -s	   <* Print score list      *>	% castle -r	   <* Recover a saved game  *>Main Command List:	h - 4 --  Turn Left		|	l - 6 --  Turn Right	j - 2 --  Back Up		|	k - 8 --  Move Forward	  .   --  Turn Around		|	c - C --  Cast Spells	q - Q --  Quit			|	i - I --  Inventory	r - R --  Rest (unimplemented)  |       d - D --  Disarm Trap	  >   --  Go Down Stairs	|         <   --  Go Up Stairs	  L   --  Lookup a spell	|	  v   --  Version	  S   --  What spells are known |         N   --  Change Name       			ctrl e --  Exit & Save A Game			ctrl r --  Redraw the screenInventory Commands:	p - P  --  Go To the Previous Inventory Item.	n - N  --  Go To the Next Inventory Item.	w - W  --  Weild An Item.	r - R  --  Take Off an Item.	d - D  --  Drop an Item.	esc    --  Exit Inventory.Combat Commands:	f - F  --  Fight Your Opponent Hand to Hand.	d - D  --  Defend Yourself (gives an effective AC bunus of +4)				   (For that round.)	r - R  --  Run away, (Success Depends on your Dexterity).	c - C  --  Cast Spells.  (See Spell list).Spell List:	a)	Tells where you where you are in the Maze.	b)	Provides You with a limited duration magical		Compass.	c)	Teleport Self.	d)  	Cure light Wounds, +5 to Hitpoints.	e)	Detect Traps, Limited duration.	f)	Cause Light wounds (1 point of damage * spell caster level).	g)      Spell cost is 5pts.  Does 5 - 20 points of		electric shock damage.  Percent failure based		on intelligence.	h)      Heal from 10-15 points of damage.	i)	Tunnel through a wall directly ahead.  Makes		Temporary Hole.  Cost is 6.	j) 	Flames a creature for 10-35 points of damage.		Cost is 8.	Rest Hmm, you see.			    The Wizards Castle	The Story:	   Many years ago an evil wizard took over the land.  He	created a dungeon of death beneath his castle.  The only	way to free the land is to kill him.  This is your mission	should you choose to take it.  All you have to go on is	a few rumors, are they true?  You have heard that the	evil wizard is in the very bottom of the dungeon and has	many monsters protecting all the levels.  The traps are	well hidden and somtimes they do things you will not	notice.  Good LUCK!!  (You will need it).	The Player Character:	   You the player character has attributes that will enable	you to fight the monsters, they include:	Str)ength     - How physically strong you are.	Dex)terity    - How fast on you feet you are. Aids in defense.	Con)stitution - How healthy you are.  Aids in resisting spells.	Int)elligence - How smart you are.  Aids in casting spells.	Wis)dom	      - How much do you know.	Other attributes:	Lvl	      - A measure of experience that governs what you		        know and how much hitpoints and spellpoints you			have.	Exp	      - When certain amounts of experience are attained			you will gain an experience level, thus giving			you a greater ability (ie. more hitpoints, spell-			points and more spells).	Spt	      - This is a measure of how much spell power you			Currently have.  The more spellpoints you have			the more powerful the spell is that you may cast.	MSp	      - This is the total number of spellpoints you can			have at your current level.	CHP	      - This is your current hitpoints, this shows how			much more damage you may take before being killed.			If this value goes below zero, you're dead.	MHP	      - The maximum number of hitpoints you can have at			your current level.	Gold	      - This the amount of money you have, this is useful			in buying goods from the store such as armor.  It		  	also permits you to heal yourself (for a price)			in the store (hitpoints, spellpoint and stats			may be restored).	AC 	      - How well are you protected. The higher the number			the better.Hints & Tips:	The best thing to do when you start is put on your armor.This is done with the (i) command, it puts you into a list of whatyou have.  After you are in the inventory you may go through thelist with the (n) or (p) commands, and when you want to wear thatitem hit (w).  If you don't put on your armor you will not beprotected from monsters at all.  Putting on you dagger will helpin doing damage to monsters.	Finding Fountains will allow you to increase your playerstats., these are important to your survival. A high DEX will allowyou to run away easier (hint, hint).  The rest of the stats aidyou in other ways. It is up to you to discover them.  Good luck.	Note on saved games, when you return you will have to puteverything back on (This will be fixed later).The Store:	There are stores located on the dungeon levels.  The store is aplace where you may heal yourself (for a price).  The store also sellssome random Item each time you enter.  Some are quite expensive.